.TH SDL_GetSystemPageSize 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetSystemPageSize \- Report the size of a page of memory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_cpuinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int SDL_GetSystemPageSize(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Different platforms might have different memory page sizes\[char46] In current times, 4 kilobytes is not unusual, but newer systems are moving to larger page sizes, and esoteric platforms might have any unexpected size\[char46]
.PP
Note that this function can return 0, which means SDL can\(aqt determine the page size on this platform\[char46] It will _not_ set an error string to be retrieved with
.BR SDL_GetError ()
in this case! In this case, defaulting to 4096 is often a reasonable option\[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the size of a single page of memory, in bytes, or 0 if SDL can\(aqt determine this information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

